(`packages/shared/src/__tests__/ks727-errorhandler-class-guard.test.ts:254-297`) was read for the backstop idiom.
**PRE-MEASURED** in a scratch clone at the tip; see `## Premises (measured)`. **This is a PARTIAL of KS-1182:** F7 (the
ks844 test's name and markers, "optional" in the ticket) is NOT in this task.

## THE MODE — read this twice

Your diff contains EXACTLY TWO files, in this order:
1. `Blockchain/Dev/services/demo-service/src/middleware/errorHandler.ts` — ONE hunk, `--- a/…` / `+++ b/…`, exactly as
   `## The exact change` gives it.
2. The NEW test file `Blockchain/Dev/services/demo-service/src/__tests__/ks1182-demo-service-errorhandler-unchecked-err-status.test.ts`
   — `--- /dev/null` then `+++ b/…`, one `@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@` hunk, every line `+`.

Do NOT modify `ks844-demo-service-mounts-no-error-handler.test.ts` (it is the reference; ignore it). Do NOT touch `app.ts`.
The checker applies the test ALONE at the untouched tip and expects the 🔴 cells RED by assertion and both 🟢 controls
